  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nA gradient between high pressure over Quebec and Josephine well\noffshore will persist over the forecast area through Friday \nmorning. Breezy northerly winds continue this evening and will \nsubside some tonight while remaining elevated. Breezy northerly\nwinds combined with cool air will bring sub freezing wind \nchills to much of the area Friday morning. Winds will start to\nrelax Friday evening as high pressure builds close to overhead.\nHigh pressure will center over the area Friday night through\nSunday bringing optimal conditions for radiational cooling. This\nwill allow for lows to drop below freezing across the area both\nFriday and Saturday night. Day time highs will moderate into the\n50s Saturday and 60s on Sunday.\n\nHigh pressure slips south Monday as a dry cold front approaches\nfrom the NW. It will be mild Monday ahead of the cold front with\nhighs in the mid to upper 60s south of the mountains. The cold\nfront crosses late Monday with high pressure returning through\nthe balance of next week. This will allow for chilly nights with\nlows in 20s and sunny but cool days with highs in the 40s and\n50s.",
